{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791743461,"nonce":"t+LUYv476neg3f2qYG4dRBgAxZo=","title":"prefs: state click slow, live preview takes 6.6s and blocks the event loop","message":"User report: clicking a state on /prefs to rank or exclude takes seconds. Measured on a copy of the real DB (2127 canonical jobs in 30 days): POST /prefs/state 3ms, the prefs-changed preview POST /prefs/preview 6.6s. cProfile: 5.5s in re.Pattern.search, 53010 calls, from prefilter.rule_credential_required (_COMPILED credential patterns over full description text), via console.prefs.prefilter_delta which evaluates every job twice (before and after profile). Second cause: preview is an async def handler doing sync DB and CPU work, so it blocks the event loop and the next state click queues behind it. Fix: make the credential rule cheap without changing any result (e.g. a cheap substring gate per credential before the regexes, and or memoize per job text, since the result does not depend on the profile), stop the preview blocking other requests (sync def or threadpool, check sqlite connection threading), and consider hx-sync replace on the preview so stacked clicks do not queue previews. Acceptance: identical prefilter results on every job in a DB copy before and after; preview well under 1s on the copy; state clicks stay responsive while a preview runs.","files":null}]}